A||||9||MontanaFiero||Door skin removal-- How in the @#*!||||8||
Z||000000||MontanaFiero||02-28-2001||05:38 PM||||Can anyone tell me how to get the door skins off of the door? I have been working on this for hours and I have disconnected everything I can possibly see that looks like it is connected to the door skin itself except for this black plastic cam lock thingy which won't turn. Does this actually hold the door skin on?<P>------------------<BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||8
Z||000001||TheFiero64||02-28-2001||05:58 PM||||There are 4 fasteners, 2 on each side of the door. They are black plastic. They take a torx bit. Then lift the door skin from the bottom and unhook the handle and lock cylender from the rods and pull up on the door skin. I think you may have to undo a 6 mm screw under the long black molding too. I can't remember. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MontanaFiero||02-28-2001||06:21 PM||||Thanks "TheFiero64", apparently it is some sort of screw under the long molding (on each end). Now to get the molding off without breaking it....||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||02-28-2001||07:19 PM||||There are 4 (I think) plastic rivets at the bottom of the door skin. These have to be knocked out.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MontanaFiero||02-28-2001||07:37 PM||||got 'em-- thanks <BR>I even got the molding off without breaking the clips- yipeee!<BR>But.... now I have almost re-installed the new door with power windows for my power window conversion on the coupe. OOOOPS, I didn't pay attention to that little arm that the spring goes on. It is on the inside of the door now and the new pins are installed. Of course the door cannot be shut this way, so looks like I'm going to be at this for a while.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> It's Montana and it's starting to cool off and get dark.<P>||||reg||7
Z||000005||speed racer||05-29-2001||08:15 PM||||can some one tell me what he means when he says knock them out||||reg||1
Z||000006||skitime||05-29-2001||09:41 PM||||The plastic rivets are easily removed by driving the center out. I use an awl. A firm blow drives the center through and the rivet head then can be pulled out. Don't use a drill becaue you might damage the panels.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||cadaver||05-29-2001||10:10 PM||||Sounds like an aweful lot of work to get power windows.<BR>I just swapped the power regulators for the non power ones when I did my upgrade.<BR>And there are 7 of those plastic fasteners. 4 along the back and 3 on the front side.<BR>If they strip or break no biggie as they are just a head cover over a regular bolt.||||reg||1
Z||000008||3400Fiero||05-30-2001||10:22 AM||||I converted my 88 coupe to power windows without completely removing the skins - just removed the fasteners on the bottom and rear, then pulled it out enough to insert the mechanism from the bottom.  Worked well.<P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC||||reg||14
Z||000009||cadaver||05-30-2001||09:27 PM||||Thats even too much work, I swapped the regulators out through the door opening. Why snap or drill the fasteners then have to replace them with something else?||||reg||1
